---
import ReportLayout from '@/components/ReportLayout.astro';
import FindingCard from '@/components/FindingCard.astro';
---

<ReportLayout title="Myprotein — Homepage">

  <section class="report-intro">
    <h1 class="report-h1">UX Audit: Myprotein Homepage</h1>
    <p class="report-meta">Myprotein Homepage &mdash; Audited 17 August 2026</p>
    <p class="report-summary">
      Focused audit of myprotein.com at desktop (1440px) and mobile (390px) viewports, run as a
      live test of the newly-installed <code>myprotein-ux-review</code> skill and its design-token
      reference file. This pass covers the hero banner, Best Sellers product carousel, Clothing
      Sale carousel, and primary CTAs at both viewports. It is a first-pass, not an exhaustive
      audit — full nav mega-menus, search, footer, and every carousel item were not individually
      checked. The standout issue is an inaccessible hero CTA baked into a static image with no
      accessible name, present at both viewports.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="findings-section">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Findings</h2>

    <!-- HIGH PRIORITY -->

    <FindingCard
      title="Hero CTA is baked into a static image with a blank accessible name"
      viewport="Both"
      priority="high"
      ticketType="engineering"
      ticketable={true}
      findingId="hero-cta-image-blank-label"
    >
      <p slot="what">
        The entire hero — headline, subhead, and the "SHOP NOW" button — is rendered as a single
        banner <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> wrapped in one <code>&lt;a&gt;</code>, at both desktop and
        mobile viewports. DOM inspection confirms the image's <code>alt</code> attribute is a
        single space character (<code>" "</code>), and the wrapping link's <code>aria-label</code>
        is also just a space. There is no real "SHOP NOW" button element in the DOM for this hero —
        it's pixels in the graphic.
      </p>
      <p slot="why">
        Screen reader users land on this link and hear nothing — not "Shop Now", not the
        destination, not even the promo. This is the first and most prominent CTA on the homepage,
        currently invisible to assistive technology (WCAG 2.1 SC 1.1.1 Non-text Content and SC 2.4.4
        Link Purpose both fail). It's also a maintenance cost: any copy change to "25% OFF" or the
        CTA label requires re-exporting an image rather than editing text, and the button doesn't
        use the real pill/button component from the design system at all.
      </p>
      <p slot="fix">
        Set a real <code>alt</code> on the image describing the promotion (e.g. "25% off almost
        everything"), and give the wrapping link a proper <code>aria-label</code> such as "Shop 25%
        off almost everything". Longer term, rebuild the hero as layered text + the real button
        component over a background image, so the CTA is an actual interactive element using the
        pill button token (radius 9999px, <code>#003942</code> fill) rather than flattened artwork.
      </p>
    </FindingCard>

    <!-- MEDIUM PRIORITY -->

    <FindingCard
      title="Large dead whitespace gaps between homepage sections on mobile"
      viewport="Mobile"
      priority="medium"
      ticketType="engineering"
      ticketable={true}
      findingId="mobile-dead-whitespace"
    >
      <p slot="what">
        Scrolling the mobile homepage (390px), there's roughly 800&ndash;900px of combined blank
        vertical space: a large empty gap below the Best Sellers product carousel and above its
        "VIEW ALL" button, and a second gap between "VIEW ALL" and the "Clothing Sale" heading
        below it. This persisted after a few seconds' wait, so it isn't just a lazy-load-in-progress
        skeleton state.
      </p>
      <p slot="why">
        On mobile, where scroll distance is already at a premium, roughly two screen-heights of
        empty space between sections adds significant, purposeless scroll effort and makes the page
        feel broken or unfinished at exactly the point where a user is browsing product carousels —
        a core conversion path.
      </p>
      <p slot="fix">
        Inspect the carousel and "VIEW ALL" wrapper elements for a fixed-height container that isn't
        collapsing to its content on mobile (a common cause is a min-height or aspect-ratio rule
        sized for a desktop layout leaking into the mobile breakpoint). Recommend re-checking this
        live, since it's the kind of layout bug worth confirming isn't specific to this one session.
      </p>
    </FindingCard>

  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Design Consistency</h2>
    <p>
      Core interactive elements match the design token reference well: the Quick Buy and hero
      buttons use Figtree, uppercase bold labels, and the correct <code>#003942</code> primary
      fill/border, and their computed border-radius (32px on a ~48px-tall button) renders as a full
      pill visually identical to the <code>9999px</code> pill token — not a real deviation. Product
      card background (<code>#f6f3ef</code>) is a close but not exact match for the documented
      <code>secondary.lightest</code> token (<code>#F8F7F4</code>) — a minor, likely imperceptible
      drift, not worth a ticket on its own.
    </p>
    <p>
      Note for context: an earlier version of this skill (before its design-token reference file
      existed) generated a prior homepage report on 2 June 2026 that raised a "Quick Buy button
      missing the mint outer ring" finding, on the assumption that a mint (<code>#94E5B5</code>)
      ring was the brand's primary CTA signature. The live-verified token data now available shows
      that's incorrect — mint is a radio/toggle selection ring, not a button signature — so that
      earlier finding (and the related hero-CTA-ring recommendation) should be treated as
      superseded, not acted on as written.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Accessibility Notes</h2>
    <p>
      The hero CTA's blank <code>alt</code>/<code>aria-label</code> (WCAG 2.1 SC 1.1.1, SC 2.4.4) is
      the significant issue found in this pass — it removes the primary homepage action from screen
      reader users entirely. By contrast, the "What's New" carousel CTA checked during this audit
      (a "SHOP NOW" link into New In clothing) does carry a correct <code>aria-label="SHOP NOW"</code>,
      showing the pattern is inconsistently applied across the page rather than a blanket policy.
      Colour contrast, focus order, and form labelling were not exhaustively checked in this pass.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Conversion Summary</h2>
    <p>
      The homepage's promotional messaging and product carousels are clear and the core buying
      controls (Quick Buy, pricing, promo badges) are well-styled and on-brand. The most consequential
      issue is invisible rather than visual: the primary hero CTA doesn't exist as far as assistive
      technology is concerned, at both viewports, which is a hard conversion blocker for those users
      rather than friction. The mobile whitespace gaps are a softer but still real tax on scroll
      effort during browsing, right where users are comparing products.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-heading">Recommended Implementation Order</h2>
    <ol class="recommendations">
      <li>Add a real <code>alt</code> and <code>aria-label</code> to the hero banner image/link at both viewports — small fix, removes a hard accessibility blocker on the page's primary CTA.</li>
      <li>Investigate and fix the mobile dead-whitespace gaps around the Best Sellers carousel and "VIEW ALL" button.</li>
      <li>Longer term: rebuild the hero as real text + button over a background image rather than flattened artwork, so copy and CTA changes don't require new image exports.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

</ReportLayout>

<style is:global>
  .finding-card code {
    font-family: Menlo, Monaco, 'Courier New', monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    background: var(--color-bg-muted);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: var(--color-text-heading);
  }
</style>

<style>
  .report-intro { margin-bottom: 40px; }
  .report-h1 { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 800; color: var(--color-text-heading); line-height: 1.25; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .report-meta { font-size: 13px; color: var(--color-text-body); opacity: 0.65; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .report-summary { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-text-body); max-width: 680px; }
  .findings-section { margin-bottom: 48px; }
  .section-heading { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--color-text-heading); margin-bottom: 20px; padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(0, 57, 66, 0.1); }
  .prose-section { margin-bottom: 36px; }
  .prose-section p { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-text-body); }
  .recommendations { padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  .recommendations li { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-text-body); }
</style>
